WEBVTT

00:01.870 --> 00:04.160
<i>I have had a long life.</i>

00:06.540 --> 00:11.170
<i>Because I've lived so long, I've learned 
that the world is beyond my control.</i>

00:13.830 --> 00:15.420
<i>So I fought.</i>

00:17.760 --> 00:22.410
<i>As ruler, as protector, as heir...</i>

00:24.230 --> 00:28.780
<i>I fought, and fought, and kept fighting...</i>

00:37.040 --> 00:39.310
Let's stop this stupid war.

00:42.720 --> 00:46.040
I'd rather sit down and have a talk with you.

00:47.520 --> 00:48.860
Setsu...

00:51.760 --> 00:53.180
Here.

00:57.100 --> 00:58.010
What is this?

01:01.320 --> 01:03.060
A token of reconciliation.

01:03.600 --> 01:06.170
I think black would look great on you, Dezas.

01:06.830 --> 01:07.990
Setsu...

01:09.730 --> 01:12.330
<i>I thought what I needed 
to do to live my life</i>

01:12.330 --> 01:16.640
<i>was give up what makes me </i>me<i>.</i>

01:22.140 --> 01:25.540
<b>Evilbarrow, the Dark Lord's Castle</b>

01:25.540 --> 01:27.350
Missing?

01:27.350 --> 01:28.020
Yes.

01:28.530 --> 01:30.540
We did all we could, but couldn't find him.

01:30.970 --> 01:35.030
It seems like Distinia has 
no idea where he is, either.

01:35.030 --> 01:36.310
Enough.

01:44.440 --> 01:50.860
<i>Even if we never meet again, I will keep
 the promise of peace I made to you...</i>

01:51.360 --> 01:52.390
Setsu.

01:54.270 --> 01:56.420
We did strike a peace deal,

01:56.420 --> 01:59.390
but there's still much to do before 
we achieve true, lasting peace.

02:00.020 --> 02:01.660
We must redouble our efforts, Vlad.

02:01.660 --> 02:05.160
Yes! I, Vlad, will lay down my life for this!

02:09.460 --> 02:10.690
Lord Dezastol!

02:11.120 --> 02:14.360
We have fresh fruit from Distinia today!

02:14.360 --> 02:18.990
My lord! The meat from my homeland 
is fresh and tasty, too!

02:21.340 --> 02:23.610
It has been five years 
since the end of the war.

02:23.610 --> 02:25.650
It's great to see our 
nation prosper like this.

02:25.650 --> 02:30.770
Yes. Everyone worked so hard. War is—

02:40.190 --> 02:41.430
My lord?

02:43.870 --> 02:47.470
Perhaps I've spent too much time wearing it.

02:49.310 --> 02:52.860
I heard there is a skilled 
jeweler in Distinia.

02:53.480 --> 02:55.610
I'll send it out for repairs.

02:55.610 --> 02:58.880
Thank you. Sorry to send 
you on a personal errand.

04:36.130 --> 04:40.960
<b><i>Episode 4</i></b>

04:36.130 --> 04:40.960
<b><i>Receiving a Gift for a Second Time</i></b>

04:48.850 --> 04:54.370
Reporting! A Distinian army has 
appeared and invaded us!

04:54.810 --> 04:58.220
Battle rages as we speak, 
just outside of Evilbarrow!

04:59.890 --> 05:02.650
Only five years after the peace charter?

05:02.650 --> 05:04.300
How frail this peace was.

05:05.240 --> 05:07.220
Let's not jump to conclusions.

05:09.380 --> 05:11.330
Gather all the top officers immediately!

05:11.840 --> 05:13.840
We will prepare our army!

05:13.840 --> 05:14.890
Yes, my lord!

05:14.890 --> 05:18.680
Zeon and Lamina, 
head to Distinia immediately.

05:18.680 --> 05:20.060
Something is suspicious.

05:20.520 --> 05:22.520
We must first find out what's going on.

05:22.520 --> 05:23.170
Yes, my lord!

05:30.080 --> 05:34.450
Setsu, I will keep our promise. 
No matter what.

05:46.110 --> 05:51.620
Weapons go in the first warehouse, food and 
medicine to the second warehouse! Hurry!

05:51.620 --> 05:53.690
We have to return to the 
front lines right away.

05:53.690 --> 05:56.250
Who knows if we'll come 
back alive this time...

05:56.250 --> 06:00.080
So there are huge, armored enemies 
that weren't there five years ago?

06:00.590 --> 06:02.960
What did we sign that peace charter for?

06:03.560 --> 06:06.840
We should never have trusted the humans.

06:07.100 --> 06:11.770
If a full-on war breaks out and 
destroys our supply chain, we'll...

06:11.770 --> 06:17.350
It's fine! As long as we buy her some time, 
the Demon Lord will take care of this.

06:19.700 --> 06:25.060
<i>Even after a month, 
there's been no contact from Distinia...</i>

06:26.570 --> 06:32.620
<i>We're holding the line for now, 
but our nation won't last long at this rate.</i>

06:33.170 --> 06:36.830
<i>Am I incapable of keeping 
my promise to Setsu?</i>

06:38.200 --> 06:39.360
Excuse me.

06:40.880 --> 06:42.880
Vlad. What is it?

06:42.880 --> 06:48.360
Terran Sneeter from the Terran Trading 
Company requests an audience with you.

06:48.800 --> 06:50.040
Terran himself?

06:50.860 --> 06:52.970
Well, I can't turn him away.

06:53.320 --> 06:54.280
Let him in.

06:54.280 --> 06:55.120
Yes, my lord.

07:01.010 --> 07:02.150
Are you crazy?!

07:02.150 --> 07:05.470
Watch what you say, lowly human!

07:05.470 --> 07:08.570
Oh, no. I am completely serious.

07:08.570 --> 07:11.320
This is a sincere offer.

07:12.070 --> 07:18.780
I would like to use the power of Terran 
Trading to help end the war with Distinia.

07:19.200 --> 07:23.330
What more could a ruler ask for?

07:23.330 --> 07:27.300
Using your wealth, purported 
to be the greatest in the world?

07:27.300 --> 07:32.670
Yes. To be honest, I feel we can end 
the war outright, not just offer help.

07:33.170 --> 07:36.540
That's how powerful the 
Terran Trading Company is.

07:46.840 --> 07:48.940
And in return, you would ask...

07:48.940 --> 07:56.200
To have you become my wife, 
Dezastol Serreno. Precisely.

07:56.820 --> 07:59.910
You must mean your <i>slave</i>.

08:01.030 --> 08:05.310
If it means having your beauty in my grasp,
 then you may call it whatever you wish.

08:06.380 --> 08:10.180
Here is the necklace on which 
we will swear our vows.

08:13.090 --> 08:16.140
A curse of servitude?! And so powerful...

08:16.360 --> 08:18.730
It seems you came well prepared.

08:19.260 --> 08:21.350
Where did you get such a thing?

08:21.660 --> 08:24.360
It did require some effort on my part,

08:24.360 --> 08:28.820
but it was all in the name of my love for you.

08:30.440 --> 08:34.780
My lord, do not even entertain such nonsense!

08:34.780 --> 08:36.570
We must immediately take this fool and—

08:37.980 --> 08:40.700
Give me some time to think.

08:40.700 --> 08:42.070
My lord!

08:44.280 --> 08:47.300
I have all the time in the world.

08:49.190 --> 08:51.180
But I wonder...

08:51.180 --> 08:53.600
Do <i>you</i> have that kind of time?

09:11.700 --> 09:16.380
Is this the only way I can 
keep my promise to you?

09:19.720 --> 09:20.740
My lord...

09:21.800 --> 09:23.750
I thought I asked everyone to leave.

09:27.240 --> 09:30.260
There's no need for you to 
accept that ridiculous offer.

09:30.920 --> 09:36.610
Your army is ready to fight to the 
last man for you, myself included.

09:38.000 --> 09:41.220
I know. That's why I can't refuse.

09:55.590 --> 09:59.950
Do you think me a foolish woman, 
unworthy of being the Demon Lord?

10:00.940 --> 10:04.140
I won't give up. Please excuse me.

10:08.930 --> 10:12.000
You told me black would look good on me.

10:12.470 --> 10:17.620
Will you laugh when you see me wear 
white against my wishes, Setsu?

10:20.730 --> 10:24.460
Dezastol was easier to 
convince than I expected.

10:25.190 --> 10:31.900
It seems lending aid to your schemes through 
the Terran Trading Company will pay off.

10:32.220 --> 10:35.280
Now the demonic kingdom is ours.

10:36.400 --> 10:40.320
If we push any further,
 we might start a tiresome war.

10:40.320 --> 10:43.210
Should we pull back those 
expensive magic soldiers?

10:44.070 --> 10:46.160
No need.

10:46.490 --> 10:53.930
Why not? You want the demonic kingdom, 
I want the beautiful Demon Lord.

10:53.930 --> 10:56.050
This deal is settled, is it not?

10:56.470 --> 10:59.340
Because it is the will of my master.

11:04.810 --> 11:10.060
<b>—Day of the Wedding—</b>

11:43.090 --> 11:44.630
So beautiful!

12:19.210 --> 12:25.340
Groom, Terran Sneeter, and bride,
 Dezastol Serreno.

12:26.250 --> 12:28.930
You may now exchange your vows of love.

12:32.810 --> 12:38.110
I, Terran Sneeter, and 
Demon Lord Dezastol Serreno,

12:38.110 --> 12:41.970
swear today to enter into a 
vow of master and servant!

12:43.020 --> 12:45.970
And the Terran Trading Company, 
through the annexation

12:45.970 --> 12:48.660
of the power of the demonic 
kingdom of Eviltheon,

12:48.970 --> 12:56.080
vows to bring eternal prosperity 
and everlasting peace to the world!

12:58.140 --> 13:00.680
Now, my compatriots!

13:00.680 --> 13:04.400
Pledge your allegiance to me,
 your new Demon Lord,

13:04.400 --> 13:09.190
and together we will protect the world 
and leave our names in the history books!

13:17.840 --> 13:21.020
Now, enough theatrics.

13:24.800 --> 13:30.280
Dezastol Serreno, you will vow 
eternal love to me, Terran.

13:48.780 --> 13:54.050
<i>If only I could see you 
one last time... Setsu...</i>

14:02.520 --> 14:03.710
Wh-What?!

14:03.710 --> 14:05.400
An explosion?! Are we under attack?!

14:20.110 --> 14:23.620
I'm here to rescue you, princess.

14:25.500 --> 14:26.520
Setsu!

14:32.820 --> 14:35.400
Vlad-san, look!

14:35.400 --> 14:36.930
That's Setsu-san, isn't it?

14:37.900 --> 14:39.770
He's as over-the-top as ever.

14:40.070 --> 14:40.960
Let's hurry.

14:42.730 --> 14:45.210
Wh-What are you?!

14:45.210 --> 14:47.130
What <i>are</i> you?!

14:50.160 --> 14:53.830
Fools! Do your job! Protect me!

15:03.810 --> 15:04.790
Levia!

15:04.790 --> 15:08.040
Dezas, you really don't look good in white.

15:08.500 --> 15:11.560
You should give up on 
wearing a wedding dress.

15:15.520 --> 15:17.560
Shadow Magic: Shadow Stab.

15:23.220 --> 15:24.270
I can't move?!

15:24.870 --> 15:28.150
The god of the seas isn't 
too impressive on land, I see.

15:34.780 --> 15:35.620
Stop!

15:52.960 --> 15:59.310
So, ready to pay for making Dezas cry?

16:01.310 --> 16:04.190
I wasn't expecting Setsu the Hero to show up.

16:04.700 --> 16:07.270
I'll have quite the report to give my master!

16:07.860 --> 16:09.150
Your master?

16:14.110 --> 16:15.170
What?!

16:29.120 --> 16:33.470
Is that it? You're not even trying.

16:34.360 --> 16:36.370
You are indeed strong,

16:36.370 --> 16:39.330
but today I must prioritize 
notifying my master.

16:40.950 --> 16:43.980
We'll settle this later, Setsu the Hero.

17:00.990 --> 17:03.230
Damn it, he got away.

17:03.230 --> 17:04.280
Setsu!

17:05.210 --> 17:08.410
I missed you! I missed you, Setsu!

17:08.410 --> 17:12.130
Where did you go without me?!

17:12.130 --> 17:16.100
Y-Yeah, that's a long story...

17:16.560 --> 17:19.640
Anyway, I'm glad you're safe, Dezas.

17:20.290 --> 17:21.090
Yes!

17:23.230 --> 17:27.150
Uh, sorry to interrupt this 
touching reunion, but...

17:36.920 --> 17:39.670
Magic soldiers made from curses...

17:44.690 --> 17:50.040
These curses... I guess it really
must be Toma behind the scenes.

17:52.800 --> 17:57.240
I suspected it might be possible. 
So it really is Toma, then.

17:57.240 --> 18:00.800
Then, as Demon Lord,
 I must lend you aid, Setsu!

18:01.260 --> 18:03.760
He needs to pay for making me wear this.

18:04.740 --> 18:08.500
I'll let you handle things here, then.
 I'll go visit Regulus.

18:09.100 --> 18:11.820
There's no telling what Toma might try.

18:12.070 --> 18:13.860
The Beastmen...

18:13.860 --> 18:18.710
Yes, securing the aid of Regulus, King of 
the Beastmen, would be most reassuring.

18:19.160 --> 18:20.990
But this all seems very rushed.

18:22.040 --> 18:24.970
We do have a promise of peace to keep.

18:24.970 --> 18:26.320
Yes.

18:27.160 --> 18:29.860
We must do this, for our promise.

18:30.960 --> 18:33.870
Wait, are we leaving right away?

18:33.870 --> 18:37.600
Am I on ferry duty again?

18:37.600 --> 18:41.760
I've been running around fighting all night!

18:41.760 --> 18:42.970
Setsu-san!

18:44.360 --> 18:49.480
Oh, no! The castle is a mess!

18:49.840 --> 18:51.490
Did everything work out?

18:51.490 --> 18:54.110
Yeah. It was pretty close, though.

18:59.240 --> 19:02.030
You should be the one to give this to her.

19:02.620 --> 19:04.490
It's important, right?

19:06.560 --> 19:08.140
Yeah, thanks.

19:12.300 --> 19:13.500
Setsu?

19:25.680 --> 19:27.470
This makes another second time.

19:32.940 --> 19:35.380
Yes, the second time.

19:49.570 --> 19:51.180
<i>That's right.</i>

19:53.030 --> 19:59.560
<i>Once again, you've taught me 
what it means to live.</i>

21:47.400 --> 21:51.800
I would have loved to accompany you,

21:51.800 --> 21:55.620
but this is no time for the 
ruler to leave her throne.

21:55.620 --> 21:59.990
Yeah. Once we get back to peace, 
I'll take you wherever you want.

22:02.610 --> 22:05.010
Yes. That's a promise.

22:05.330 --> 22:11.390
Well, um... Just because it's peacetime 
doesn't mean the ruler can leave the country...

22:11.740 --> 22:14.630
That's where you come in.

22:15.150 --> 22:17.410
Don't make Dezas do all the work.

22:17.410 --> 22:18.070
Yes.

22:18.850 --> 22:24.260
The Demon Lord kindly allowed 
me to open a shop here!

22:24.260 --> 22:26.650
My very own shop! It's my dream come true!

22:26.870 --> 22:28.060
Are you sure?

22:28.060 --> 22:32.090
She delivered my precious brooch.
It's the least I could do.

22:34.650 --> 22:36.710
Thanks for the help, Setsu.

22:37.400 --> 22:41.020
If you need anything,
 we will race to your side.

22:41.020 --> 22:43.810
Yeah. I'll be counting on you.

22:48.610 --> 22:50.980
All right, ready to go?

22:50.980 --> 22:52.930
Oh, very well.

22:52.930 --> 22:56.430
I'll tag along with you, no matter how far!

22:56.790 --> 22:57.670
Yeah!

23:05.020 --> 23:11.950
Be sure to come straight 
back to me once it's all over!

23:17.190 --> 23:19.020
Yeah, see you soon!

23:26.920 --> 23:31.930
<b><i>Next Time</i></b>

23:26.920 --> 23:31.930
<b><i>Following Footsteps for a Second Time</i></b>

23:27.790 --> 23:31.040
Next time: "Following 
Footsteps for a Second Time."
